The hardening evidence is decisive even though the quota expired before the script could write a terminal verdict: 11 of 12 scored bare attempts solved across \(p=29,37,47,97\), including all three at \(p=97\). The intended nullspace insight is visible enough that the models execute it unaided. I’m therefore recording an H/Track-B rejection, retaining the built generator under the required `rejected_gen_…` name, and preserving the script-owned transcript.
