   158	question = render(inst)
   159	candidate = parse_answer('<answer>{"normals":[[1,1,1,1],[1,1,1,1]]}</answer>')
   160	ok, reason = verify(inst, candidate)
   161	```
   162	
   163	From the repository root, after a successful bare hardening rerun, emit instances with:
   164	
   165	```bash
   166	bash scripts/emit.sh 1111.3517 20 easy
   167	```
   168	
   169	To finish the presently blocked requirement, replenish or replace `OPENROUTER_API_KEY`, rerun `python3 ../../scripts/harden.py gen_1111_3517.py` here, and rerun the structural/placebo copies in separate scratch directories as prescribed by the task.
   170	
   171	## Caveats
   172	
   173	- This is Track B, not evidence that Roman domination or efficient domination is easy or hard on the generated distribution. The disclosed Python scan solves the declared symbolic language in seconds (0.971 seconds on average in the saved run).
   174	- The instance is an exact implicit graph, not an expanded adjacency list. The product at shipping size has about \(5\times10^{11}\) vertices; the polynomial Cayley presentation and hyperplane witness are essential to keeping posing and checking finite.
   175	- `P(random guess)` is uniform over pairs of normalized projective directions. It removes zero vectors and scalar duplicates, but it is not a prior over arbitrary Roman functions. The exact density applies only to the certificate language explicitly requested by the statement.
   176	- The adversary panel tried coefficient-energy outliers, coordinate projection, linear-term and leading-term ansatzes, and 256 random restarts. It did not run SAT/ILP or exact cover on the expanded graph, which is infeasible to materialize. The strongest applicable symbolic scan is disclosed as the successful Track B reference algorithm.
   177	- The canonical key handles ambient invertible linear-coordinate changes (tested through generators), parameter scaling, factor exchange, and compositions. It may fail to identify an exotic nonlinear isomorphism or a set-equivalent polynomial reparameterization outside this generated symmetry group; full Cayley-graph isomorphism is not attempted.
   178	- There may be multiple valid hyperplane normals on some seeds. `verify` accepts all of them, and G5 counts them exactly at the shipping measurement seed. The recorded shipping instance had five valid directions in factor 0 and two in factor 1, hence ten valid pairs; the demo has four valid pairs.
   179	- Most importantly, the required oracle hardness evidence is missing because of external quota exhaustion. Do not treat `SHIPPING_DIFFICULTY="easy"` as a completed release decision until the three harness arms produce scored attempts.

